WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:05.259
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, this week for
my Game of Thrones video I’m going to talk

00:00:05.259 --> 00:00:10.019
about ancient Valyria and the future of the
Targaryen’s in book form.

00:00:10.019 --> 00:00:11.860
Martin has teased that he really wants to
write a Fire and Blood compendium after he’s

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:16.680
done with A Song of Ice And Fire. It would
be a complete historical record of the Targaryen

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:23.680
Family from Ancient Valyria to Daenerys, it
might even extend past her lifetime.

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:28.470
We don’t really know what her fate is in
the books. But if you’ve read any of his

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:32.730
short stories, I think it will read like those
instead of the POV style that the Song of

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:34.540
Ice and Fire novels have.

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:39.810
Real quick reminder, I’m doing a weekly
World of Ice and Fire book giveaway. All you

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:43.310
have to do to enter is be a subscriber and
leave a comment.

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:47.510
So just general spoiler warning for everything
on the show so far and everything up to book

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:51.940
4. That’s pretty much where the show is
right now, with a few exceptions.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:57.100
Starting with a breakdown of the rise of Valyria.
World of Ice and Fire adds some nice context

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:02.180
to what was previously discussed in the regular
novels. Coolest fact: Dragons, at one time

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:03.510
covered the earth.

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:07.470
They weren’t like a swarm of locusts or
anything, just imagine how as predators they

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:11.330
flourished during a pre-historic period when
geographical conditions were favorable and

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:12.860
they were the apex predators.

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:17.520
There have been dragon bones found all over
the world, not just in the warmer part of

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:18.970
Westeros and the Eastern Continent.

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:24.740
They are critical to the rise of Valyria but
they predate Valyrians by a long long time.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:29.610
Valyrians, as we know, discovered them roosting
in the Fourteen Flames. The peninsula of Volcanoes

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:34.159
here at the south of the Eastern Continent.
This is the area that became The Valyrian

00:01:34.159 --> 00:01:34.820
Freehold.

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:40.650
That took a long time, even though the books
make it sound like an overnight thing. Think

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:45.009
of the Valyrians learning to bond with Dragons
like the Dothraki domestication of Horses.

00:01:45.009 --> 00:01:49.850
It’s not the same thing. Dragons were never
domesticated. But as close as you can get

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:51.930
to domesticating Dragons.

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:55.799
As that started to happen Valyrians socially
became a much more isolated group of people.

00:01:55.799 --> 00:01:59.770
If you had the world’s greatest super weapons
you’d probably start acting a little xenophobic.

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:04.409
That’s why over time Valyrians developed
certain genetic characteristics like the Silver-Gold

00:02:04.409 --> 00:02:05.930
Hair and Purple eyes.

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:10.349
The show changed the eyes. The Producers said
that Purple eyes didn’t look good on camera

00:02:10.349 --> 00:02:15.700
so they had to drop that bit about Daenerys
and Viserys.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:18.450
Some of you may also have noticed how some
of the characters hair colors have changed

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:23.030
just a little since the pilot episode. Tyrion
is the biggest change. He went from Lannister

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:25.000
Blonde to a much dirtier mix.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.840
Not a huge deal, it was only weird the first
time I saw it and then by the time season

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:31.880
4 rolled around last year I wasn’t even
thinking about it anymore.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:36.540
So over time the Valyrians are mastering Dragons
with a combination of Blood and Fire Magic,

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:43.540
Enchanted Items, like the dragon horns and
Sorcery.

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:47.330
The show hasn’t really addressed this in
detail but I do think by the time season 6

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:53.690
and 7 are here they will. As we get on in
the seasons characters like Samwell, Tyrion,

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:56.950
Varys, they’ll probably be given most of
that exposition.

00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:03.290
Jon Snow is awesome when it comes to brooding,
but he’s not the scholar that Samwell is.

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:07.930
My only minor complaint about the books so
far is that the mechanics of how Valyrians

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:14.930
tamed dragons and what it has to do with their
blood is still a mystery. But affinity with

00:03:17.989 --> 00:03:24.580
Dragons became a genetic thing. Which is why
the Valyrians practiced selective breeding.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:29.750
That raises all kinds of issues like the increased
risk of negative genetic anomalies but The

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:32.870
Doom took care of that problem.

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:39.870
One 
of the most critical periods of time during
the rise of Valyria was it’s war with the

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:47.870
Ghiscari Empire. Before Valyria expanded all
over the eastern continent. The Ghiscari Empire

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:48.970
was the greatest civilization.

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:53.060
Right now where we are on the show you only
see their legacy in the architecture around

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:57.470
Slaver’s Bay. But as we spend more time
in Meereen during Season 5 we’ll probably

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:01.400
get a better look at the really cool buildings.
The Pyramid and the fighting pits are only

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:02.450
the beginning.

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:05.879
The Valyrians warred back and forth with the
Ghiscari in five great battles. After the

00:04:05.879 --> 00:04:10.470
fifth battle the Valyrians razed all the land
and plowed it with salt so that the Ghiscari

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:13.819
would never be able to grow crops again. And
that was the end of them.

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:20.819
Valyrian expansion continued unchecked, but
they kept one really important aspect of Ghiscari

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:23.849
Culture. Slavery.

00:04:23.849 --> 00:04:30.629
They started taking slaves from all over their
Empire to work the mines near the fourteen

00:04:30.629 --> 00:04:37.629
flames. The fourteen flames are a series of
volcanoes, so they bring up all kinds of precious

00:04:42.189 --> 00:04:49.189
metals and ore from the earth. So the area
around Valyria was very literally a gold mine.

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:56.300
But that’s also where they mined the ore
for creating Valyrian Steel.

00:04:56.300 --> 00:05:01.939
Their empire wasn’t ruled by a single individual,
it was much more democratic. Every great family

00:05:01.939 --> 00:05:06.930
had a vote. But during really important periods
sometimes they’d appoint a single decision

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:07.009
maker.

00:05:07.009 --> 00:05:09.149
And in order to consolidate their power throughout
the empire sometimes they’d arrange political

00:05:09.149 --> 00:05:09.589
marriages with the locals. Or if cities wouldn’t
do what they wanted, they’d appoint an archon

00:05:09.589 --> 00:05:10.270
to rule there, to make sure everything ran
smoothly.

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:12.909
So even though Valyrians guarded their bloodlines
closely, they’d still marry people off to

00:05:12.909 --> 00:05:13.949
neighboring rulers if necessary.

00:05:13.949 --> 00:05:18.339
Later in their expansion, the Valyrians inspired
the creation of the Free Cities as well as

00:05:18.339 --> 00:05:25.339
migration to Westeros. Qohor and Norvos, which
are right here were founded during religious

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:33.460
schisms, Old Volantis and Lys right here were
orginally created to be Trading colonies set

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:37.430
up by wealthy merchants who had purchased
the right to rule as clients of the Valyrian

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:37.930
Freehold.

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:44.930
In doing so, those cities were allowed to
appoint their own rulers.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:52.509
In other cases some cities like Pentos and
Lorath, which are right here, chose to pay

00:05:52.509 --> 00:05:56.689
tribute when the Valyrian’s came with their
dragons. So they were allowed to retain the

00:05:56.689 --> 00:05:59.869
infrastructure as long as they kept paying
tribute.

00:05:59.869 --> 00:06:02.179
One of the few exceptions to all these situations
was Braavos, it’s story is kind of unofficial.

00:06:02.179 --> 00:06:05.149
In the books it’s told as if characters
aren’t sure it’s true. So it’s canon.

00:06:05.149 --> 00:06:10.020
But the story is that a couple of Valyrian
slave ships were sailing in the narrow sea.

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:14.139
The Valyrians used slave labor so the slaves
outnumbered the Valyrians and mutinied. I

00:06:14.139 --> 00:06:18.559
guess the valyrians in charge didn’t have
any dragons with them at the time.

00:06:18.559 --> 00:06:21.929
The slaves were so afraid of the Freehold
coming after them that they sailed to where

00:06:21.929 --> 00:06:24.279
modern day Braavos is and created a secret
city. For hundreds of years they remained

00:06:24.279 --> 00:06:26.119
secret before revealing themselves to the
world, after the Doom.

00:06:26.119 --> 00:06:28.990
But because the original settlers were slaves
taken from all over the empire, they all had

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:32.919
different customs and different gods. That’s
why today there are so many shrines to different

00:06:32.919 --> 00:06:33.649
gods in Braavos.

00:06:33.649 --> 00:06:37.879
We will see some of the city. I don’t know
how many episodes will spend there in season

00:06:37.879 --> 00:06:41.229
5, but there’s an area in the middle of
town here where you can find the biggest temples.

00:06:41.229 --> 00:06:43.689
All to different gods.

00:06:43.689 --> 00:06:49.979
So Braavos, the Free Cities all part of the
Rise of Valyria and a big part of it’s legacy.

00:06:49.979 --> 00:06:55.289
I’ll spend more time talking about different
cities specifically in future bonus videos

00:06:55.289 --> 00:06:58.360
so be sure to subscribe to get everything.
And be sure to let me know which ones you

00:06:58.360 --> 00:07:02.259
want to talk about first.

00:07:02.259 --> 00:07:06.990
The rest of Valyria’s history is a little
more well known. The Doom of Valyria was a

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:09.479
cataclysm like the eruption of Vesuvius on
Pompeii.

00:07:09.479 --> 00:07:15.550
Think about it this way. Vesuvius was just
one volcano, Valyria had 14. So when they

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:20.439
say Doom, it was Hell on Earth.

00:07:20.439 --> 00:07:27.439
There’s a lot of theories about what caused
The Doom, I think it was a combination of

00:07:28.909 --> 00:07:33.520
the Valyrians Over-Mining the Volcanoes, there
were geographical changes happening naturally

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:36.129
and I think there was a little bit of magic
involved.

00:07:36.129 --> 00:07:38.949
Just a confluence of events that blew the
shit out of the peninsula here.

00:07:38.949 --> 00:07:44.419
The Targaryen’s we know escaped after Danearys
the Dreamer had a vision of the Doom, her

00:07:44.419 --> 00:07:51.419
father sold all the families assets in the
freehold and moved everything they had along

00:07:52.789 --> 00:07:56.770
with five Dragons to Dragonstone.

00:07:56.770 --> 00:08:01.379
Only one of those dragons survived to the
time of Aegon the Conqueror, Balerion the

00:08:01.379 --> 00:08:08.379
Black Dread. But eventually more dragons were
hatched and the rest we can talk about in

00:08:10.289 --> 00:08:14.099
another bonus video.

00:08:14.099 --> 00:08:20.899
Let me know if you think we’ll see characters
from the show travel to where Valyria used

00:08:20.899 --> 00:08:21.659
to be ever.

00:08:21.659 --> 00:08:24.939
George RR Martin has already confirmed there
will be more flashbacks to ancient valyria.

00:08:24.939 --> 00:08:28.009
But he hasn’t promised that we’ll travel
there in present day.

00:08:28.009 --> 00:08:29.849
Just more awesome things to look forward too.

